  "description": "The same provider_message_id redelivered with a different subject line raises IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT.",
  "why_it_exists": "Inbound delivery is at-least-once. Without a stored ingress fingerprint a redelivered message either appended a duplicate inbound row and a duplicate action, or - once a wall-clock value entered the fingerprint - a plain retry looked like a tampered message and raised a false IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT. The fingerprint is now derived only from the raw message, and every replay outcome is decided before the classifier runs. The subject is part of the fingerprint basis, so an edited subject is a changed message. Suite case X2.",
